WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:15.486
Brad: But, Danny, how is a candle going to help?

2
00:00:15.487 --> 00:00:17.299
Danny: What do you mean?

3
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:18.964
Brad: It’s not lit.

4
00:00:18.965 --> 00:00:21.222
How are we going to light it?

5
00:00:21.223 --> 00:00:25.168
Danny: What if I make a flame out of yellow clay?

6
00:00:25.169 --> 00:00:26.879
Tina: Try it, Danny!

7
00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:30.525
Danny: Okay. Tina, you hold the candle for me.

8
00:00:30.526 --> 00:00:33.847
Tina: Don’t take too long.

9
00:00:33.848 --> 00:00:38.311
Danny: There!

10
00:00:38.312 --> 00:00:45.187
Brad: I-I t-told y-you it wouldn’t w-w-work.

11
00:00:45.188 --> 00:00:48.544
Danny: Yes, it will. We just have to concentrate.

12
00:00:48.545 --> 00:00:51.093
Danny: Imagine that the flame is burning.

13
00:00:51.094 --> 00:00:53.775
Danny: That’s how we made the doors appear.

14
00:00:53.776 --> 00:00:57.394
Tina: And how we escaped from the squishy soil.

15
00:00:57.395 --> 00:00:59.484
Brad: Okay. Let’s try.

16
00:00:59.485 --> 00:01:02.925
I don’t want to freeze again!

17
00:01:02.926 --> 00:01:13.505
Danny: Concentrate really hard. Ready? Go!

18
00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:15.891
Danny: Awesome! We did it!

19
00:01:15.892 --> 00:01:19.080
Tina: Let’s hope it’s hot enough to melt this snow!

20
00:01:19.081 --> 00:01:23.058
Brad: That’s a pretty small flame.

21
00:01:23.059 --> 00:01:25.319
Danny: Just give it a minute.

22
00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:27.609
Tina: It’s not helping much.

23
00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:29.191
Danny: But we have fire.

24
00:01:29.192 --> 00:01:32.487
We must be able to use it.

25
00:01:32.488 --> 00:01:36.559
Brad: Just give me one minute.

26
00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.533
Brad: Here, I found it!

27
00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:42.787
Brad: Danny, help me gather some flat shiny pieces of ice.

28
00:01:42.788 --> 00:01:44.567
Danny: Why?

29
00:01:44.568 --> 00:01:46.095
Brad: I’ll show you.

30
00:01:46.096 --> 00:01:48.600
Pass me that piece by your foot there.

31
00:01:48.601 --> 00:01:52.530
Brad: Thanks. I just need five or six pieces.

32
00:01:52.531 --> 00:01:55.758
Tina: Whatever you’re doing, Brad, do it quickly.

33
00:01:55.759 --> 00:01:58.840
Tina: My arm is beginning to ice up again!

34
00:01:58.841 --> 00:02:00.917
Brad: I’m making a curved mirror.

35
00:02:00.918 --> 00:02:03.670
Brad: I found instructions on my computer.

36
00:02:03.671 --> 00:02:07.499
Brad: We just place the ice in a circle, like this.

37
00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:12.932
Brad: Then lean the pieces at a 45-degree angle. There!

38
00:02:12.933 --> 00:02:16.496
Brad: Now place the candle in the center, Tina.

39
00:02:16.497 --> 00:02:20.646
Danny: Let’s hope this works!

40
00:02:20.647 --> 00:02:28.269
Tina: Look, the roof is melting.

41
00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:31.036
Brad: I’m feeling warmer already!

42
00:02:31.037 --> 00:02:36.585
Danny: Look how fast the snow is melting now!

43
00:02:36.586 --> 00:02:39.995
Tina: Hey, Danny! Doesn’t that look like a leaf?

44
00:02:39.996 --> 00:02:47.702
Danny: Yes! And there’s a flower over there!

45
00:02:47.703 --> 00:02:49.544
Danny: This is so cool!

46
00:02:49.545 --> 00:02:52.101
There are hundreds of flowers.

47
00:02:52.102 --> 00:02:55.661
Brad: I wonder what kind of world this is.

48
00:02:55.662 --> 00:02:58.026
Tina: I hope it’s the giants’ world.

49
00:02:58.027 --> 00:03:01.464
If it isn’t, it’s probably dangerous.

50
00:03:01.465 --> 00:03:08.506
Danny: Well, let’s find out if it is the giants’ world.

51
00:03:08.507 --> 00:03:10.699
Danny: Hopian?

52
00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:14.300
Tina: Danny, I don’t see any giants wandering around.

53
00:03:14.301 --> 00:03:17.278
Brad: Maybe there’s a clue somewhere.

54
00:03:17.279 --> 00:03:20.330
Tina: Let’s go explore.
